Z||000000||frontal lobe||09-26-2000||02:54 PM||||Well, I sold my white '86gt 4-speed manual this weekend.  Bought it about a year ago with the intent of putting a v8 in it.  Ran fine for about a week after I bought it, and then developed a (loud) rod knock and would barely run.  One thing after another, long sob story, blah, blah, and v8 conversion wasn't going to happen.  Who wants a Fiero with a bad engine?  Apparently a lot of people because I got a lot of calls.  First guy wanted to buy it for a parts car.  Why?  Because he already has THREE white '86gt's!!! out of his stable of 26 cars (inc. 3 1950's era t-birds and a '67 vette.  Life is tough).  So he comes to see the car and says it's too nice to be a parts car so he is going to have his mechanic fix it and run it.  So I sold the car, but didn't feel too bad since it is going to a good home where it will be loved and appreciated.  I love a happy ending.||||reg||1
